1
00:00:05,080 --> 00:00:06,920
(Highlights. Golden Key rankings)
How many golden keys does everyone have?

2
00:00:07,280 --> 00:00:09,040
(Warning)
Don't ask. You won't like the answer.

3
00:00:09,040 --> 00:00:11,040
They rank from the lowest.

4
00:00:11,040 --> 00:00:12,760
Ning might break the record.

5
00:00:12,760 --> 00:00:13,360
Really?

6
00:00:13,360 --> 00:00:16,040
Yeah, no one had over seven keys
in past seasons.

7
00:00:16,040 --> 00:00:17,520
We should add a rap part to this song.

8
00:00:17,960 --> 00:00:18,840
♪I want golden keys♪

9
00:00:18,840 --> 00:00:19,560
♪Give me the golden keys♪

10
00:00:19,560 --> 00:00:20,880
(Starting with a bang)
♪How many golden keys do I have now?♪

11
00:00:20,880 --> 00:00:22,160
Teach me a few dance moves.

12
00:00:22,740 --> 00:00:24,060
(Easy to handle)

13
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:26,120
So cool.

14
00:00:26,120 --> 00:00:28,080
(Puzzling the level)
It should move.

15
00:00:28,080 --> 00:00:29,800
(Manual push)
Yeah, it might push us later.

16
00:00:30,360 --> 00:00:31,640
(Drooling)
What is this?

17
00:00:31,640 --> 00:00:33,880
It's mochi. It's super delicious.

18
00:00:34,320 --> 00:00:35,800
(Turn to open)
Try another one.

19
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:37,200
(Trying everyone's birthdays)
Zero, one, zero, eight.

20
00:00:37,520 --> 00:00:39,480
(That's too simple)
Would they really set it like this?

21
00:00:39,480 --> 00:00:40,320
Zero, seven, zero, one.

22
00:00:40,720 --> 00:00:41,840
Zero, four, zero, two.

23
00:00:41,840 --> 00:00:42,720
Just force it.

24
00:00:42,840 --> 00:00:45,360
(Food feast, everyone eats)
We got one step wrong.

25
00:00:45,960 --> 00:00:47,560
(Completely reversed)
Who puts the sausage on the outside?

26
00:00:47,560 --> 00:00:48,360
(Not bad)
It's okay.

27
00:00:48,620 --> 00:00:50,080
(Let me try too)

28
00:00:50,080 --> 00:00:51,520
(Calling for help)
What should I do? Ning, help me.

29
00:00:51,700 --> 00:00:53,580
(Chef Ning's online tutorial)

30
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:54,560
It smells so good.

31
00:00:54,900 --> 00:00:55,780
(I want some)

32
00:00:57,920 --> 00:00:59,040
You think it's just right, right?

33
00:00:59,040 --> 00:01:00,640
The sauce will make it too salty.

34
00:01:00,880 --> 00:01:01,440
Everyone,

35
00:01:01,440 --> 00:01:02,280
we're about to leave.

36
00:01:02,280 --> 00:01:03,080
Okay.

37
00:01:03,420 --> 00:01:05,100
(Take a quick bite)

38
00:01:06,420 --> 00:01:10,220
=Truth Clubhouse=

39
00:01:10,260 --> 00:01:12,540
(Last Struggle for the Golden Key)

40
00:01:14,440 --> 00:01:16,560
(Singing mode)
♪I can't let him go♪

41
00:01:16,560 --> 00:01:17,640
♪I can't♪

42
00:01:18,680 --> 00:01:20,680
I saw you on the red carpet today.

43
00:01:20,680 --> 00:01:21,440
I have a whole storyline.

44
00:01:21,440 --> 00:01:22,880
Can you tell?

45
00:01:22,880 --> 00:01:23,800
What's the storyline?

46
00:01:23,800 --> 00:01:25,280
(Straight into character)
I came out looking unhappy.

47
00:01:25,280 --> 00:01:26,120
The bad girl.

48
00:01:26,120 --> 00:01:26,800
Someone is taking pictures!

49
00:01:26,800 --> 00:01:27,980
(Paparazzi shots)

50
00:01:28,100 --> 00:01:29,740
(Respect)

51
00:01:29,960 --> 00:01:31,600
You couldn't tell the storyline?

52
00:01:31,600 --> 00:01:32,200
(Honest.jpg)
Nope, I couldn't.

53
00:01:32,700 --> 00:01:34,120
(Always training)

54
00:01:34,120 --> 00:01:36,480
How many golden keys does everyone have?

55
00:01:36,480 --> 00:01:38,640
(Warning)
Don't ask. You won't like the answer.

56
00:01:38,640 --> 00:01:40,360
(Playful He)
They rank from the lowest.

57
00:01:40,360 --> 00:01:41,160
(Playful Ke)
Start with the lowest.

58
00:01:41,160 --> 00:01:42,000
Who's at the bottom?

59
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:42,680
Who's the lowest?

60
00:01:42,680 --> 00:01:43,360
(Think before answering)

61
00:01:43,360 --> 00:01:44,080
I don't know.

62
00:01:44,600 --> 00:01:45,480
(I hope you really don't know)
I don't know either.

63
00:01:45,480 --> 00:01:46,440
Being the highest doesn't matter.

64
00:01:46,440 --> 00:01:47,880
(Harmless but brutal)
We're actually at the bottom.

65
00:01:47,880 --> 00:01:48,600
It's hard to guess.

66
00:01:48,600 --> 00:01:49,680
(Kicking while down)
Who is this?

67
00:01:50,320 --> 00:01:51,160
Too hard.

68
00:01:51,160 --> 00:01:52,080
Forget those two.

69
00:01:52,080 --> 00:01:53,240
(Slightly annoyed)
They're always like this.

70
00:01:53,240 --> 00:01:54,000
But you suddenly act like this.

71
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:54,960
I can't handle it.

72
00:01:54,960 --> 00:01:55,920
I'm not, Jin.

73
00:01:55,920 --> 00:01:57,280
(Give me another chance)
My bad.

74
00:01:57,280 --> 00:01:58,320
You always stand aside.

75
00:01:58,320 --> 00:01:59,440
Just laughing.

76
00:01:59,440 --> 00:02:00,280
Now you're in charge.

77
00:02:00,280 --> 00:02:00,880
I'll kneel.

78
00:02:00,880 --> 00:02:01,860
(Show respect)

79
00:02:02,360 --> 00:02:03,800
How many do you have?

80
00:02:03,800 --> 00:02:05,120
I have...

81
00:02:06,200 --> 00:02:07,000
Four.

82
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:08,880
What about me? How many do I have?

83
00:02:08,880 --> 00:02:10,000
Two? Three?

84
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:11,400
How many does Ning have?

85
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:11,800
Don't ask.

86
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:12,320
Don't.

87
00:02:12,320 --> 00:02:14,080
Just tell me.

88
00:02:14,080 --> 00:02:16,000
(Full of curiosity)
I really want to know how many he has.

89
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:16,960
(Curiosity +1)
Ning, how many do you have?

90
00:02:16,960 --> 00:02:18,680
If we count everything he got...

91
00:02:18,680 --> 00:02:19,480
Six?

92
00:02:19,480 --> 00:02:20,960
(White lie)
No, four.

93
00:02:20,960 --> 00:02:22,880
(No way)
No way. You definitely have five.

94
00:02:22,880 --> 00:02:24,480
Six wins out of eight.

95
00:02:24,480 --> 00:02:25,720
Who has six wins?

96
00:02:26,380 --> 00:02:27,180
Hahaha!

97
00:02:28,120 --> 00:02:30,040
Ning might break the record.

98
00:02:30,040 --> 00:02:30,480
Really?

99
00:02:30,480 --> 00:02:31,200
Yeah.

100
00:02:31,200 --> 00:02:32,640
No one had over seven keys

101
00:02:32,640 --> 00:02:33,600
in past seasons.

102
00:02:33,600 --> 00:02:35,800
(Scarily strong)
You already have six.

103
00:02:35,800 --> 00:02:36,720
Only two keys left.

104
00:02:36,720 --> 00:02:37,840
One today, one tomorrow.

105
00:02:37,840 --> 00:02:39,760
Yeah, if you win every day.

106
00:02:39,760 --> 00:02:40,560
It seems like...

107
00:02:40,560 --> 00:02:42,040
You still can't catch up to me.

108
00:02:42,060 --> 00:02:42,660
(Killing with words moment)

109
00:02:43,280 --> 00:02:44,600
Thanks for explaining.

110
00:02:44,600 --> 00:02:45,720
Yeah.

111
00:02:45,760 --> 00:02:47,520
Look Jin, next season.

112
00:02:47,520 --> 00:02:48,800
(Offering some comfort)
Keep trying next season.

113
00:02:48,800 --> 00:02:49,480
Daniel.

114
00:02:49,480 --> 00:02:51,600
(Forced smile)
Thank you so much.

115
00:02:51,600 --> 00:02:52,320
You're welcome.

116
00:02:54,040 --> 00:02:55,240
(One celebrates, one breaks)
Glad to have you.

117
00:02:57,620 --> 00:03:00,220
(Ding joins)

118
00:03:00,720 --> 00:03:02,280
How many does Ding have now?

119
00:03:02,280 --> 00:03:03,120
How many keys do you have?

120
00:03:03,120 --> 00:03:04,360
Four.

121
00:03:04,360 --> 00:03:04,920
Everyone has four.

122
00:03:04,920 --> 00:03:06,360
Looks like we all have four.

123
00:03:06,360 --> 00:03:07,720
Then the three of us are tied.

124
00:03:07,720 --> 00:03:08,760
(Proud)

125
00:03:08,760 --> 00:03:10,080
Ning has the most.

126
00:03:10,080 --> 00:03:10,960
Yeah, six.

127
00:03:10,960 --> 00:03:12,960
Your hairstyle looks great today.

128
00:03:12,960 --> 00:03:13,400
Really?

129
00:03:13,460 --> 00:03:14,260
(Hit the right taste point)

130
00:03:15,240 --> 00:03:15,640
Alright.

131
00:03:15,640 --> 00:03:18,400
Let's go back to our investigation.

132
00:03:18,400 --> 00:03:19,000
Okay.

133
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:20,120
Let's go.

134
00:03:21,440 --> 00:03:23,400
♪Come now, players all♪

135
00:03:27,440 --> 00:03:28,120
What should we do?

136
00:03:29,600 --> 00:03:31,000
Are we supposed to look straight ahead?

137
00:03:32,280 --> 00:03:32,880
Sure.

138
00:03:32,880 --> 00:03:33,920
Anything works.

139
00:03:33,920 --> 00:03:35,400
It's like we're ready to face death.

140
00:03:35,400 --> 00:03:36,000
Kidding.

141
00:03:37,920 --> 00:03:39,200
♪Come now, players all♪

142
00:03:39,200 --> 00:03:41,360
♪Let the game of reason start♪

143
00:03:41,360 --> 00:03:43,320
♪Unlock the mystery, turn the question♪

144
00:03:43,320 --> 00:03:44,640
♪Let courage spark the dark♪

145
00:03:45,520 --> 00:03:46,840
♪Come now, players all♪

146
00:03:47,520 --> 00:03:48,840
♪Let the game of reason start♪

147
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:01,120
We should add a rap part to this song.

148
00:04:01,120 --> 00:04:02,600
(Starting with a bang)
♪I want golden keys♪

149
00:04:02,600 --> 00:04:03,880
♪How many golden keys do I have now?♪

150
00:04:03,880 --> 00:04:05,760
You can do a solo part.

151
00:04:05,760 --> 00:04:08,440
We'll give you a separate section.

152
00:04:08,440 --> 00:04:09,800
Like...

153
00:04:09,800 --> 00:04:11,320
Something like Nicki Minaj.

154
00:04:11,320 --> 00:04:12,520
Can you rap?

155
00:04:12,520 --> 00:04:13,400
Not really.

156
00:04:13,400 --> 00:04:15,040
You should ask him. He can.

157
00:04:15,040 --> 00:04:16,360
(All-rounder Ding)
You can rap too?

158
00:04:16,360 --> 00:04:17,400
I can't rap.

159
00:04:17,400 --> 00:04:18,520
He's just being humble.

160
00:04:18,520 --> 00:04:19,560
Do an English rap.

161
00:04:19,560 --> 00:04:21,440
♪One, two, three, four♪

162
00:04:21,780 --> 00:04:23,740
(Perfect comedic timing)

163
00:04:23,760 --> 00:04:24,840
Teach me a few dance moves.

164
00:04:26,900 --> 00:04:29,380
(Easy to handle)

165
00:04:31,680 --> 00:04:33,040
So cool.

166
00:04:33,060 --> 00:04:35,020
(Learning)

167
00:04:36,400 --> 00:04:39,040
(Eager to learn)
Teach me that footwork you did earlier.

168
00:04:39,040 --> 00:04:39,840
It's easy.

169
00:04:39,840 --> 00:04:41,120
(Flexible moves)
C-Walk.

170
00:04:41,120 --> 00:04:41,600
One.

171
00:04:43,680 --> 00:04:44,960
No, it's just one foot.

172
00:04:44,960 --> 00:04:46,000
This one goes outward.

173
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:46,640
This goes outward.

174
00:04:47,640 --> 00:04:48,720
This one goes inward.

175
00:04:48,720 --> 00:04:49,680
Use your toes here.

176
00:04:49,680 --> 00:04:50,600
Use your heel here.

177
00:04:51,400 --> 00:04:52,760
Right, then bring it back.

178
00:04:53,940 --> 00:04:54,940
(Unlocking a new skill)

179
00:04:55,960 --> 00:04:56,960
Right.

180
00:04:56,960 --> 00:04:57,760
It's kinda hard.

181
00:04:58,140 --> 00:05:00,420
(Unlocking is our specialty)

182
00:05:00,520 --> 00:05:01,600
(Night vision mode)
Are we going to the teleport pod?

183
00:05:01,600 --> 00:05:02,520
Just go straight in?

184
00:05:02,520 --> 00:05:03,000
Go in.

185
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:03,520
Let's go.

186
00:05:08,760 --> 00:05:10,560
It should move.

187
00:05:10,560 --> 00:05:12,640
(Manual push)
Yeah, it might push us later.

188
00:05:12,640 --> 00:05:13,360
Come here.

189
00:05:13,360 --> 00:05:15,480
(Empty spot here)
Stand here.

190
00:05:15,480 --> 00:05:16,120
Stand over there.

191
00:05:16,120 --> 00:05:17,440
Who's older between you two?

192
00:05:17,440 --> 00:05:18,600
(Proud)
I'm older.

193
00:05:18,600 --> 00:05:19,160
Is he older?

194
00:05:19,160 --> 00:05:19,920
He's older.

195
00:05:19,920 --> 00:05:21,120
I'm older.

196
00:05:22,480 --> 00:05:23,240
Tastes good, right?

197
00:05:23,240 --> 00:05:24,440
This is good.

198
00:05:24,440 --> 00:05:25,360
I wasn't eating that one.

199
00:05:26,680 --> 00:05:27,960
(Drooling)
What is this?

200
00:05:27,960 --> 00:05:29,160
It's mochi.

201
00:05:29,160 --> 00:05:29,920
It's super delicious.

202
00:05:30,760 --> 00:05:31,440
Is this really that good?

203
00:05:31,440 --> 00:05:32,680
(Snack lover)

204
00:05:32,680 --> 00:05:33,720
My bun is gone.

205
00:05:34,760 --> 00:05:36,080
Your bun is gone?

206
00:05:36,080 --> 00:05:37,040
Just take one.

207
00:05:37,040 --> 00:05:38,120
We're about to be pushed away.

208
00:05:42,780 --> 00:05:44,940
(Charging)

209
00:05:47,160 --> 00:05:48,600
Are we pushing it over manually?

210
00:05:48,600 --> 00:05:48,960
Yes.

211
00:05:50,200 --> 00:05:51,560
Lift us up to the sky.

212
00:05:51,560 --> 00:05:52,800
I remember that time.

213
00:05:54,080 --> 00:05:54,560
Lift it up?

214
00:05:54,560 --> 00:05:55,680
Did they hang it up by hand?

215
00:05:55,680 --> 00:05:56,400
No, with a crane.

216
00:05:56,400 --> 00:05:58,680
They put us in a container before.

217
00:05:58,680 --> 00:06:00,360
(Curious mind kicking in)
Do you think this can be opened?

218
00:06:00,360 --> 00:06:02,360
Yeah, what's the password?

219
00:06:02,360 --> 00:06:03,360
It should open from the back.

220
00:06:03,360 --> 00:06:05,280
I recently learned a new skill.
Lockpicking.

221
00:06:05,280 --> 00:06:06,560
(Main: Singer, Actor. Side: Lock King)
For this show.

222
00:06:06,560 --> 00:06:07,400
I can open it. Really.

223
00:06:07,400 --> 00:06:07,720
Really?

224
00:06:07,720 --> 00:06:08,480
(Still skeptical)
You actually learned it?

225
00:06:08,480 --> 00:06:08,840
Yes, I did.

226
00:06:08,840 --> 00:06:10,280
Where did you learn that?

227
00:06:10,280 --> 00:06:11,240
I really can open it.

228
00:06:11,240 --> 00:06:12,240
(It's time to show my skills)
Go ahead. Open it.

229
00:06:12,240 --> 00:06:13,080
Let me see.

230
00:06:14,880 --> 00:06:16,320
You're so professional, Ning.

231
00:06:17,160 --> 00:06:18,480
Did you film
a crime investigation drama?

232
00:06:18,480 --> 00:06:19,360
That's why you learned this?

233
00:06:22,240 --> 00:06:22,720
(Failed to unlock)
Nope.

234
00:06:22,720 --> 00:06:23,160
I can't open it.

235
00:06:23,860 --> 00:06:25,340
(Ke getting excited)

236
00:06:25,440 --> 00:06:26,520
(Let me try too)
I'll give it a try.

237
00:06:27,760 --> 00:06:28,560
(Turn to open)
Try another one.

238
00:06:29,200 --> 00:06:30,920
(Trying everyone's birthdays)
Zero, one, zero, eight.

239
00:06:30,920 --> 00:06:32,320
Would they really set it like this?

240
00:06:32,800 --> 00:06:33,280
What if they did?

241
00:06:33,280 --> 00:06:33,840
Zero, one, zero, eight.

242
00:06:35,200 --> 00:06:35,920
Try another one.

243
00:06:35,920 --> 00:06:36,560
(Glad it was wrong)
You scared me.

244
00:06:36,560 --> 00:06:37,320
One, one, zero, two.

245
00:06:37,320 --> 00:06:38,080
You scared me.

246
00:06:38,080 --> 00:06:39,200
One, two, three, zero, right?

247
00:06:39,200 --> 00:06:40,920
If you actually guess it like this...

248
00:06:40,920 --> 00:06:43,080
I'm impressed.

249
00:06:43,080 --> 00:06:44,880
Let's see who can guess it blindly.

250
00:06:44,880 --> 00:06:45,920
(Everyone wants a turn)

251
00:06:45,920 --> 00:06:46,640
Zero, seven, zero, one.

252
00:06:46,640 --> 00:06:47,440
It must be related to the game.

253
00:06:47,440 --> 00:06:48,360
Why?

254
00:06:48,360 --> 00:06:50,000
(Logical reasoning)
Because it's seven plus one.

255
00:06:51,320 --> 00:06:52,040
Okay.

256
00:06:52,760 --> 00:06:54,280
Try zero, four, zero, two.

257
00:06:54,280 --> 00:06:54,840
Why?

258
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:57,200
(Still logical)
Four guys and two girls.

259
00:06:58,800 --> 00:06:59,680
So that's how you do it?

260
00:06:59,680 --> 00:07:00,440
(New password idea)

261
00:07:00,440 --> 00:07:01,120
Just force it.

262
00:07:02,540 --> 00:07:03,620
(Still trying)

263
00:07:03,640 --> 00:07:04,240
Like this.

264
00:07:05,220 --> 00:07:07,340
(Pure luck)

265
00:07:07,520 --> 00:07:09,320
You're pretty creative, Jin Jing.

266
00:07:09,320 --> 00:07:09,880
What if it works?

267
00:07:09,900 --> 00:07:11,460
(Still hoping for luck today)

268
00:07:11,520 --> 00:07:12,760
Do you really want

269
00:07:12,760 --> 00:07:13,840
to use all your luck on this?

270
00:07:16,200 --> 00:07:17,320
Your hand is already shaking.

271
00:07:18,400 --> 00:07:20,440
I've held it up for almost a month.

272
00:07:21,680 --> 00:07:22,920
Won't this part

273
00:07:22,920 --> 00:07:24,120
get bigger?

274
00:07:24,120 --> 00:07:25,600
Because you keep using it.

275
00:07:25,600 --> 00:07:27,160
No, muscles need repeated training.

276
00:07:27,160 --> 00:07:28,320
They will shrink.

277
00:07:28,320 --> 00:07:29,760
And you need resistance.

278
00:07:29,760 --> 00:07:31,520
Moving it without weight does nothing.

279
00:07:32,720 --> 00:07:34,320
(Thoughtful Jin)
Does it get pressed while you sleep?

280
00:07:34,320 --> 00:07:35,400
No, I put it on a pillow.

281
00:07:35,400 --> 00:07:36,160
This is how he sleeps.

282
00:07:39,080 --> 00:07:40,400
I use a tall pillow.

283
00:07:40,400 --> 00:07:41,360
I place it beside me.

284
00:07:41,360 --> 00:07:42,320
Then you won't turn over?

285
00:07:42,320 --> 00:07:43,040
I won't turn over.

286
00:07:43,040 --> 00:07:43,360
Hug a pillow.

287
00:07:43,360 --> 00:07:44,200
You don't move when you sleep?

288
00:07:44,200 --> 00:07:44,640
That's impressive.

289
00:07:44,640 --> 00:07:46,440
No, I do move in my sleep.

290
00:07:46,440 --> 00:07:46,960
But I...

291
00:07:47,480 --> 00:07:47,920
You got this.

292
00:07:47,920 --> 00:07:49,000
After I got this...

293
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:49,920
You became aware of it.

294
00:07:49,920 --> 00:07:51,920
Once you're aware,
before you fall asleep,

295
00:07:51,920 --> 00:07:53,240
(Muscle memory formed)
you tell yourself not to turn over.

296
00:07:53,240 --> 00:07:53,920
Here's an easier way.

297
00:07:53,920 --> 00:07:56,040
(Creative idea incoming)
Just tie a rope to the headboard.

298
00:07:58,960 --> 00:07:59,800
(Ning is too funny)
That's too cruel.

299
00:07:59,800 --> 00:08:00,280
Too cruel.

300
00:08:00,280 --> 00:08:00,800
That's cruel.

301
00:08:00,800 --> 00:08:02,040
Just tie yourself up like this.

302
00:08:02,040 --> 00:08:03,040
(Eyes locked on target)
Use handcuffs.

303
00:08:03,040 --> 00:08:04,760
What if I turn over?

304
00:08:04,760 --> 00:08:06,040
Why is there blood on your hand?

305
00:08:06,040 --> 00:08:07,060
(Suspicious discovery)

306
00:08:08,240 --> 00:08:09,080
I have it too.

307
00:08:10,120 --> 00:08:11,040
Actually, I have it too.

308
00:08:11,040 --> 00:08:11,980
(I have it too)

309
00:08:12,640 --> 00:08:13,360
Me too.

310
00:08:13,640 --> 00:08:14,800
(Found during investigation)
Only the two of us don't have it.

311
00:08:14,800 --> 00:08:16,600
I think the people without blood

312
00:08:16,600 --> 00:08:18,200
(Becoming suspicious)
are actually more suspicious.

313
00:08:18,200 --> 00:08:18,960
I don't have it.

314
00:08:18,960 --> 00:08:19,960
In my heart.

315
00:08:19,960 --> 00:08:20,760
Your heart bleeds.

316
00:08:21,800 --> 00:08:24,200
Today, it's a choice between two.

317
00:08:24,200 --> 00:08:25,320
Again? Who are we choosing?

318
00:08:25,320 --> 00:08:26,680
These two. The ones with no blood.

319
00:08:26,680 --> 00:08:27,960
Why not him?

320
00:08:27,960 --> 00:08:28,760
Yeah, why not him?

321
00:08:28,760 --> 00:08:29,920
Yeah, why not me?

322
00:08:29,920 --> 00:08:30,720
He looks like the killer today.

323
00:08:31,220 --> 00:08:33,460
(It's all my fault for talking too much)

324
00:08:33,500 --> 00:08:35,740
(Is growing up about being independent?)

325
00:08:35,840 --> 00:08:36,720
Have you ever had hot spicy strips?

326
00:08:36,720 --> 00:08:37,800
I've never had hot spicy strips.

327
00:08:37,800 --> 00:08:38,520
They're so good.

328
00:08:38,520 --> 00:08:39,220
(Delicious)

329
00:08:39,400 --> 00:08:41,120
They're even burnt.

330
00:08:41,120 --> 00:08:41,920
Ning, you worked hard.

331
00:08:41,920 --> 00:08:42,680
(Jin's concern)
I'm fine.

332
00:08:42,680 --> 00:08:43,240
It's pretty fun.

333
00:08:43,240 --> 00:08:45,480
