557
00:14:37,640 --> 00:14:37,840
Come on.

558
00:14:37,840 --> 00:14:38,600
Let's get into position.

559
00:14:38,600 --> 00:14:40,000
We'll form a circle.

560
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:40,920
(Rehearsal formation)
Step forward.

561
00:14:40,920 --> 00:14:42,640
Then we'll do it together.

562
00:14:43,520 --> 00:14:44,880
Then we'll turn like this.

563
00:14:44,880 --> 00:14:46,280
(Familiar move)
Just turn clockwise like this.

564
00:14:46,280 --> 00:14:47,080
That should work. Then...

565
00:14:47,080 --> 00:14:48,280
I think we should do this.

566
00:14:48,280 --> 00:14:49,160
(Fully committed)

567
00:14:49,160 --> 00:14:49,920
Our backs.

568
00:14:49,920 --> 00:14:51,120
Make a circle with our backs.

569
00:14:51,120 --> 00:14:51,640
Okay, good.

570
00:14:51,640 --> 00:14:53,240
Then spread outward.

571
00:14:53,240 --> 00:14:54,880
Because you know it and they don't.

572
00:14:54,880 --> 00:14:55,960
I don't really know it either.

573
00:14:55,960 --> 00:14:57,760
Right, so let Ding do it.

574
00:14:57,760 --> 00:14:59,160
Ding and you.

575
00:14:59,160 --> 00:15:00,120
(Lead dancer)
You two lead.

576
00:15:00,120 --> 00:15:01,160
I don't know it either.

577
00:15:01,160 --> 00:15:02,560
I only know a little.

578
00:15:02,560 --> 00:15:03,400
Stop pretending.

579
00:15:03,400 --> 00:15:05,040
(Don't be modest)
You've done this on "Hello Saturday".

580
00:15:05,040 --> 00:15:05,880
How could you not know it?

581
00:15:05,880 --> 00:15:07,360
But I really don't.

582
00:15:07,360 --> 00:15:08,080
Hey kid.

583
00:15:08,080 --> 00:15:08,920
Stop searching.

584
00:15:08,920 --> 00:15:10,360
You'll have plenty of time later.

585
00:15:10,360 --> 00:15:13,040
(Uncontrollable curiosity)
There's nothing here now. Trust me.

586
00:15:13,080 --> 00:15:13,880
Okay, let's go.

587
00:15:13,880 --> 00:15:15,000
Let's arrange our spots.

588
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:16,200
Come on, Ding, lead us.

589
00:15:16,200 --> 00:15:17,600
I can't dance either.

590
00:15:17,600 --> 00:15:18,960
Then learn behind her.

591
00:15:18,960 --> 00:15:19,560
You two lead.

592
00:15:19,560 --> 00:15:21,560
The four of us stay in the back. Okay.

593
00:15:21,560 --> 00:15:22,480
We'll be at the back.

594
00:15:22,480 --> 00:15:23,000
You know it?

595
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:23,640
I don't.

596
00:15:23,640 --> 00:15:23,880
Come on.

597
00:15:23,880 --> 00:15:26,510
(Get familiar with it)
♪I don't have time to shout out loud♪

598
00:15:26,510 --> 00:15:28,140
- ♪A little messy♪
- Right.

599
00:15:28,140 --> 00:15:30,000
(Group following along)
♪A little slow♪

600
00:15:32,680 --> 00:15:32,960
Okay.

601
00:15:34,020 --> 00:15:35,620
(Flower hand wave)

602
00:15:35,680 --> 00:15:36,200
What does that mean?

603
00:15:36,200 --> 00:15:36,960
It's okay. You can do it.

604
00:15:36,960 --> 00:15:37,880
(Encouraging teaching)
Perfect. Amazing.

605
00:15:37,880 --> 00:15:38,080
Good.

606
00:15:38,080 --> 00:15:38,440
Okay.

607
00:15:38,440 --> 00:15:40,240
Our house happens to have voice control.

608
00:15:40,240 --> 00:15:41,720
Come on. Three, two, one.

609
00:15:41,720 --> 00:15:42,760
Music!

610
00:15:42,980 --> 00:15:45,740
(Scene music loading)
♪I don't have time♪

611
00:15:45,760 --> 00:15:46,840
Wait, are we really singing ourselves?

612
00:15:47,140 --> 00:15:48,180
(Scene music failed)

613
00:15:48,840 --> 00:15:49,720
There's no music.

614
00:15:51,320 --> 00:15:53,880
I've heard acapella singing,
but never acapella dancing.

615
00:15:53,880 --> 00:15:54,440
Acapella dancing.

616
00:15:54,440 --> 00:15:55,740
(Completely ridiculous)
♪I don't have time♪

617
00:15:55,740 --> 00:15:57,800
(Acapella dancing is easy too)
♪To shout out loud♪

618
00:15:57,800 --> 00:15:59,540
♪A little messy♪

619
00:15:59,540 --> 00:16:01,440
(Freestyle)
♪A little slow♪

620
00:16:01,440 --> 00:16:04,820
(Lost in the moment)
♪I realized promises were lies♪

621
00:16:04,820 --> 00:16:05,580
(Going with the flow)

622
00:16:05,840 --> 00:16:06,920
How do we dance?

623
00:16:06,920 --> 00:16:07,880
I only know this part.

624
00:16:07,880 --> 00:16:09,220
(Breaking the routine)

625
00:16:09,560 --> 00:16:10,640
I know this one too.

626
00:16:10,640 --> 00:16:11,920
I know it too.

627
00:16:11,920 --> 00:16:12,440
Kids,

628
00:16:12,440 --> 00:16:15,240
your acapella dance has its own charm.

629
00:16:16,480 --> 00:16:17,720
Okay, then show us once.

630
00:16:17,720 --> 00:16:19,200
(Lead us through it)
Let's go through it once.

631
00:16:19,200 --> 00:16:20,880
Come on. One, two.

632
00:16:20,880 --> 00:16:26,560
One, two, three, four,
five, six, seven, eight.

633
00:16:26,560 --> 00:16:27,400
My head hurts.

634
00:16:27,400 --> 00:16:29,600
(Some dance tips)
My brain hurts.

635
00:16:29,600 --> 00:16:31,840
Five, six, seven, eight.

636
00:16:31,840 --> 00:16:34,600
Three, two, three, four, five.

637
00:16:34,600 --> 00:16:36,800
(Everyone dancing randomly)
Just turn around once, right? Okay.

638
00:16:36,800 --> 00:16:38,720
Four, two, three, four.

639
00:16:38,720 --> 00:16:39,400
Let's finish it.

640
00:16:39,400 --> 00:16:41,000
Five, six, seven, eight.

641
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:44,600
Then one, two, three, four, five, six.

642
00:16:44,600 --> 00:16:45,320
So cool.

643
00:16:46,300 --> 00:16:47,220
(Boxing-style swings)

644
00:16:47,840 --> 00:16:48,280
Okay.

645
00:16:48,280 --> 00:16:49,120
Nice!

646
00:16:49,120 --> 00:16:49,760
That's about it, right?

647
00:16:49,760 --> 00:16:50,640
(Everyone learned it, right?)

648
00:16:50,640 --> 00:16:51,760
Do it solo now.

649
00:16:51,760 --> 00:16:52,320
Do it solo? I can't follow.

650
00:16:52,320 --> 00:16:52,760
Hurry, come on.

651
00:16:52,760 --> 00:16:53,080
Yes, I can follow.

652
00:16:53,080 --> 00:16:54,920
(Mimicking your dance)
Ready, go.

653
00:16:54,920 --> 00:16:57,840
(Change move)
One, two, three, four.

654
00:16:57,940 --> 00:16:59,100
(Already confused)

655
00:16:59,480 --> 00:17:01,240
One, two, three, four.

656
00:17:05,880 --> 00:17:09,640
One, two, three, four,
five, six, seven, eight.

657
00:17:09,640 --> 00:17:13,040
Two, two, three, four,
five, six, seven, eight.

658
00:17:13,300 --> 00:17:14,420
(You're really having fun)

659
00:17:14,520 --> 00:17:15,440
You got the essence. Like this.

660
00:17:20,320 --> 00:17:21,040
Okay, come on.

661
00:17:21,040 --> 00:17:22,680
(Repeating it)
Guys, our house has voice control.

662
00:17:22,680 --> 00:17:24,040
It's super high-tech.

663
00:17:24,040 --> 00:17:25,120
Smart home, come on.

664
00:17:25,120 --> 00:17:27,000
Three, two, one. Music.

665
00:17:55,400 --> 00:17:57,040
Okay, just shake around.

666
00:17:57,040 --> 00:17:58,080
Shake however you want.

667
00:17:58,080 --> 00:17:58,480
Okay.

668
00:17:58,480 --> 00:17:59,800
Mom and Dad, are you satisfied?

669
00:17:59,820 --> 00:18:01,820
(Can't get enough)

670
00:18:01,840 --> 00:18:04,040
My hand is already like this,

671
00:18:04,040 --> 00:18:05,400
but I still want to keep dancing.

672
00:18:05,400 --> 00:18:06,320
(Going all out)
You danced so well.

673
00:18:07,020 --> 00:18:09,300
(Send your address,
let's exchange specialties)

674
00:18:09,320 --> 00:18:10,080
Do you think it's me?

675
00:18:10,080 --> 00:18:11,080
Vote for me, or take my surname.

676
00:18:11,620 --> 00:18:13,140
(Going against all logic)

677
00:18:13,540 --> 00:18:14,440
(Thinking of what to make up)

678
00:18:14,440 --> 00:18:15,200
Ding.

679
00:18:15,200 --> 00:18:17,280
My name has Ding in it too, okay?

680
00:18:17,280 --> 00:18:18,840
The bottom part of Ning is Ding.

681
00:18:20,420 --> 00:18:21,420
(Brain loading)

682
00:18:21,560 --> 00:18:22,640
The bottom of Ning is...

683
00:18:22,640 --> 00:18:23,360
Remove the cover.

684
00:18:23,360 --> 00:18:26,480
My name is Ning, right?

685
00:18:26,480 --> 00:18:27,960
Then I remove the top part.

686
00:18:27,960 --> 00:18:28,880
I'll be surnamed Ding.

687
00:18:28,880 --> 00:18:29,900
(Big imagination)

688
00:18:31,600 --> 00:18:32,600
How is it? I'm counting on you today.

689
00:18:35,440 --> 00:18:39,000
I feel like today might be tough.

690
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:39,600
Is it hard?

691
00:18:41,120 --> 00:18:42,920
Do you have someone in mind?

692
00:18:42,920 --> 00:18:44,040
Normally speaking,

693
00:18:44,040 --> 00:18:46,360
He hasn't been chosen for so long.

694
00:18:46,360 --> 00:18:47,880
(He should get a turn)
There are only two episodes left.

695
00:18:47,880 --> 00:18:49,560
I think he's only been chosen once.

696
00:18:50,520 --> 00:18:51,640
(What's the secret?)
What are you two talking about?

697
00:18:53,800 --> 00:18:55,280
(Count me in)
What's the secret?

698
00:18:55,280 --> 00:18:56,160
No.

699
00:18:56,160 --> 00:18:58,360
We were talking
about who it might be today.

700
00:18:58,360 --> 00:18:59,040
Who?

701
00:18:59,040 --> 00:19:00,640
(Listening carefully)

702
00:19:00,640 --> 00:19:01,760
Who do you think it is?

703
00:19:01,760 --> 00:19:03,760
Let's eliminate one first.

704
00:19:03,760 --> 00:19:04,400
Eliminate?

705
00:19:05,280 --> 00:19:07,120
Did you understand what he said?

706
00:19:07,120 --> 00:19:08,400
Ding, why are you so naughty?

707
00:19:08,400 --> 00:19:09,280
You can't bully me.

708
00:19:11,120 --> 00:19:12,360
Did you eat the peaches?

709
00:19:12,360 --> 00:19:12,720
What?

710
00:19:12,720 --> 00:19:13,680
Peaches.

711
00:19:13,680 --> 00:19:14,600
No.

712
00:19:14,600 --> 00:19:15,080
The ones you bought?

713
00:19:15,080 --> 00:19:15,760
Yeah.

714
00:19:15,760 --> 00:19:17,400
Thanks, the handsome from Wu Xi.

715
00:19:17,400 --> 00:19:18,800
My parents brought them.

716
00:19:18,800 --> 00:19:19,760
Thanks, Mr. and Mrs. Zhang.

717
00:19:19,760 --> 00:19:20,760
They're from your hometown?

718
00:19:20,760 --> 00:19:21,520
They're from mine.

719
00:19:21,520 --> 00:19:22,120
Then we have to try them.

720
00:19:22,120 --> 00:19:23,160
Because I was saying

721
00:19:23,160 --> 00:19:25,040
we always get Dandong strawberries,

722
00:19:25,040 --> 00:19:26,280
(Foodie DNA)
but we've never had Wu Xi peaches.

723
00:19:26,280 --> 00:19:27,560
She gave me a hint.

724
00:19:27,560 --> 00:19:30,120
(Supporting He)
I've never had Shanghai soup dumplings.

725
00:19:30,120 --> 00:19:31,280
How am I supposed to get them to you?

726
00:19:31,280 --> 00:19:32,120
Chongqing...

727
00:19:32,960 --> 00:19:34,440
(I get it)
Chongqing hot pot base.

728
00:19:34,440 --> 00:19:36,200
I didn't even get two packs
of hot pot base.

729
00:19:36,200 --> 00:19:36,880
(Give me your address)
I have to send it to you.

730
00:19:36,880 --> 00:19:37,840
Later, we'll do this.

731
00:19:37,840 --> 00:19:38,800
In the group chat,

732
00:19:38,800 --> 00:19:39,640
everyone sends their address.

733
00:19:39,640 --> 00:19:41,880
Let's see who sends
the most gifts to whom.

734
00:19:41,880 --> 00:19:42,520
Okay.

735
00:19:42,520 --> 00:19:44,120
(Sounds good)
Someone already sent an address.

736
00:19:44,120 --> 00:19:45,840
Tell us how much you received.

737
00:19:45,840 --> 00:19:47,440
I still haven't finished eating them.

738
00:19:47,440 --> 00:19:48,440
(Spoiled with gifts)
You bought him snacks, right?

739
00:19:48,440 --> 00:19:49,960
I bought him lots of snacks.

740
00:19:49,960 --> 00:19:51,120
Like beef crisps and stuff.

741
00:19:51,120 --> 00:19:51,840
Beef crisps.

742
00:19:51,840 --> 00:19:53,760
That's why he loves
those snacks so much.

743
00:19:53,760 --> 00:19:54,560
The ones I bought you taste better

744
00:19:54,560 --> 00:19:55,760
(Bonus question)
or the beef crisps here better?

745
00:19:55,760 --> 00:19:57,120
(Definitely yours are better)
Yours are better.

746
00:19:57,120 --> 00:19:57,680
Really.

747
00:19:57,680 --> 00:19:58,280
What kind are they?

748
00:19:58,280 --> 00:19:59,560
(Ning has tried them too)
The wasabi flavor?

749
00:19:59,560 --> 00:20:00,360
There are many flavors.

750
00:20:00,360 --> 00:20:02,920
Those beef crisps are the long strips.

751
00:20:02,920 --> 00:20:04,160
I chewed so much my jaw muscles grew.

752
00:20:04,380 --> 00:20:05,660
(Come here)

753
00:20:05,860 --> 00:20:07,860
(So comfortable)

754
00:20:09,160 --> 00:20:10,680
My necklace snagged my skin.

755
00:20:10,680 --> 00:20:11,920
I didn't pinch your necklace.

756
00:20:11,920 --> 00:20:13,600
No, it got stuck there by itself.

757
00:20:14,040 --> 00:20:14,840
Your grip is too strong.

758
00:20:14,840 --> 00:20:16,240
Actually, I really am pretty strong.

759
00:20:16,240 --> 00:20:16,800
Watch me.

760
00:20:18,440 --> 00:20:19,440
(Testing. Removing the ring)
Let me try.

761
00:20:20,760 --> 00:20:22,480
I'll just hold tight.

762
00:20:22,480 --> 00:20:23,640
Use all your strength.

763
00:20:23,640 --> 00:20:24,600
Harder.

764
00:20:24,600 --> 00:20:25,120
Come on.

765
00:20:25,900 --> 00:20:27,540
(Face really showing the effort)

766
00:20:27,560 --> 00:20:29,920
The grip is pretty strong.

767
00:20:29,920 --> 00:20:31,200
Actually, they're the strong ones.

768
00:20:31,200 --> 00:20:32,480
Be careful with the ring.

769
00:20:32,480 --> 00:20:33,840
The ring might hurt.

770
00:20:33,840 --> 00:20:34,440
You can't squeeze like that.

771
00:20:35,160 --> 00:20:37,080
We're about to start filming.

772
00:20:37,080 --> 00:20:37,920
No strength left.

773
00:20:37,920 --> 00:20:38,640
Okay.

774
00:20:38,640 --> 00:20:39,680
Your grip is definitely stronger.

775
00:20:39,680 --> 00:20:40,960
Mine isn't that strong.

776
00:20:40,960 --> 00:20:41,800
Mine really isn't.

777
00:20:41,800 --> 00:20:42,280
Use more force.

778
00:20:42,280 --> 00:20:42,640
I...

779
00:20:43,340 --> 00:20:44,300
(Ding doesn't dare)

780
00:20:45,080 --> 00:20:46,560
You're so tall.

781
00:20:46,560 --> 00:20:47,680
We've always been this tall.

782
00:20:47,680 --> 00:20:49,920
Do your feet stick out of the bed?

783
00:20:49,920 --> 00:20:51,960
Yeah. My feet usually stick
out of hotel beds.

784
00:20:51,960 --> 00:20:53,560
What's your actual height?

785
00:20:53,560 --> 00:20:54,560
I'm six foot two.

786
00:20:54,560 --> 00:20:55,360
Still six foot two?

787
00:20:55,360 --> 00:20:55,960
Yeah, six foot two.

788
00:20:55,960 --> 00:20:57,080
(Can he grow more?)
Can you still shoot up?

789
00:20:57,080 --> 00:20:58,320
(He's still growing)
He's still shooting up.

790
00:20:58,320 --> 00:20:58,880
No.

791
00:20:58,880 --> 00:21:00,440
It just changes sometimes.

792
00:21:00,440 --> 00:21:02,040
Let me ask you,
do you think they're too tall?

793
00:21:02,040 --> 00:21:02,280
Yes.

794
00:21:02,280 --> 00:21:03,840
When I first met him yesterday,

795
00:21:03,840 --> 00:21:05,360
he was filming a commercial.

796
00:21:05,360 --> 00:21:07,600
I said I looked like
a figurine standing next to him.

797
00:21:07,600 --> 00:21:08,200
How tall are you?

798
00:21:08,200 --> 00:21:08,920
I'm five foot five.

799
00:21:08,920 --> 00:21:11,240
She's actually pretty tall among girls.

800
00:21:11,240 --> 00:21:11,960
(Showing approval)
Five foot five.

801
00:21:11,960 --> 00:21:13,040
But yesterday, next to you,

802
00:21:13,040 --> 00:21:13,840
I looked like a figurine.

803
00:21:13,840 --> 00:21:14,760
I'm five foot eight.

804
00:21:14,760 --> 00:21:16,000
(Did I hear that right?)
You're five foot eight?

805
00:21:17,000 --> 00:21:17,520
(Joking)
Don't.

806
00:21:17,520 --> 00:21:18,360
I'm five foot four.

807
00:21:19,600 --> 00:21:20,600
That's the same height as my mom.

808
00:21:21,140 --> 00:21:22,900
(One generation older)

809
00:21:23,600 --> 00:21:24,960
I think I know something.

810
00:21:27,240 --> 00:21:28,920
(Teleport pod has arrived)
We're upstairs and downstairs.

811
00:21:28,920 --> 00:21:29,520
Did you guys smell

812
00:21:29,520 --> 00:21:30,520
broad beans?

813
00:21:30,520 --> 00:21:32,640
(So fragrant)
Yeah, it's their boxed meal.

814
00:21:32,640 --> 00:21:33,040
Nan.

815
00:21:38,800 --> 00:21:40,400
You're looking so seriously.

816
00:21:40,400 --> 00:21:41,280
I'm just pretending.

817
00:21:41,680 --> 00:21:42,830
It's upside down.

818
00:21:42,830 --> 00:21:46,390
Hahaha!

819
00:21:47,320 --> 00:21:49,120
(Laughing so hard)
You're really funny.

820
00:21:50,120 --> 00:21:51,160
It's upside down.

821
00:21:51,820 --> 00:21:54,100
(Wish for an after-work chat session)

822
00:21:56,620 --> 00:21:57,700
(Like)

823
00:21:58,000 --> 00:21:59,360
(What does it mean?)
Is this sarcasm again?

824
00:21:59,360 --> 00:22:00,200
This is called being smart.

825
00:22:00,920 --> 00:22:03,280
Let Nan have a highlight moment too.

826
00:22:03,280 --> 00:22:05,200
Let me have a highlight moment.

827
00:22:05,200 --> 00:22:05,880
Is it him?

828
00:22:06,880 --> 00:22:08,200
I don't know.

829
00:22:08,200 --> 00:22:09,240
Look.

830
00:22:09,240 --> 00:22:09,960
We all do this.

831
00:22:11,080 --> 00:22:12,600
Think back carefully.

832
00:22:12,600 --> 00:22:14,080
Everything that happened just now.

833
00:22:14,080 --> 00:22:15,080
It must be Li Fei.

834
00:22:15,820 --> 00:22:17,340
(Chengxin approves)

835
00:22:17,520 --> 00:22:19,800
(Feeling excited)
I'm Li Fei, no backbone.

836
00:22:19,800 --> 00:22:20,520
Unmoved by gain or loss.

837
00:22:20,520 --> 00:22:21,440
Unmoved by gain or loss,

838
00:22:21,440 --> 00:22:22,840
joy or sorrow.

839
00:22:23,640 --> 00:22:24,480
Li Fei, Li Fei.

840
00:22:24,480 --> 00:22:25,800
Taking off soon.

841
00:22:25,800 --> 00:22:26,920
A few drinks, I'm through.

842
00:22:26,920 --> 00:22:28,200
I'll be kicking up dust too.

843
00:22:28,680 --> 00:22:29,440
Is it Li Fei?

844
00:22:30,940 --> 00:22:31,660
(You're amazing)

845
00:22:31,880 --> 00:22:32,400
Why do I feel

846
00:22:32,400 --> 00:22:33,640
a little woody fragrance?

847
00:22:33,640 --> 00:22:35,200
It's wood, sandalwood.

848
00:22:35,200 --> 00:22:38,400
So is it sandalwood or a woody scent?

849
00:22:38,400 --> 00:22:40,360
Whose perfume is so fragrant today?

850
00:22:40,360 --> 00:22:41,560
Mine.

851
00:22:41,560 --> 00:22:43,000
Wait Ke, you...

852
00:22:43,000 --> 00:22:45,920
(Ginseng drink)
You're young. Do you really need this?

853
00:22:45,920 --> 00:22:47,120
I only drink two a day.

854
00:22:48,160 --> 00:22:49,400
One in the morning, one at night.

855
00:22:49,400 --> 00:22:51,120
You don't need to drink this much.

856
00:22:51,120 --> 00:22:52,320
I'm used to it.

857
00:22:53,680 --> 00:22:55,160
Dessert has arrived.

858
00:22:55,160 --> 00:22:57,040
(AirDrop)
Everyone, you can replenish your energy.

859
00:22:57,040 --> 00:22:58,680
Thanks. I've already eaten a lot.

860
00:23:00,480 --> 00:23:01,480
It's tasty, right?

861
00:23:01,480 --> 00:23:01,840
Yeah

862
00:23:01,840 --> 00:23:02,600
What is this?

863
00:23:02,600 --> 00:23:04,320
This one. This is super delicious.

864
00:23:04,340 --> 00:23:06,620
(Food in the fridge looks amazing)

865
00:23:06,800 --> 00:23:07,400
What's this?

866
00:23:07,400 --> 00:23:08,320
(Curious duo)
What's this?

867
00:23:08,320 --> 00:23:10,600
Are the guys over there
still touching them?

868
00:23:10,600 --> 00:23:11,800
I've been watching you.

869
00:23:11,800 --> 00:23:13,280
Are you still touching them?

870
00:23:13,280 --> 00:23:14,320
That might not be a good idea.

871
00:23:14,320 --> 00:23:15,320
(Strong lift)
It fell.

872
00:23:16,640 --> 00:23:17,480
Miss, I'm eating this.

873
00:23:17,480 --> 00:23:18,080
Take it away from me.

874
00:23:19,920 --> 00:23:20,480
Sour plum.

875
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:21,680
(Sharing a snack)
Really?

876
00:23:24,720 --> 00:23:26,040
(Not bad)
I'm okay with sour stuff.

877
00:23:26,040 --> 00:23:27,600
I love sour food.

878
00:23:27,600 --> 00:23:28,840
This dried yogurt is really good.

879
00:23:28,840 --> 00:23:29,400
You can have a piece.

880
00:23:29,400 --> 00:23:30,640
I already ate it.

881
00:23:30,640 --> 00:23:32,160
Did you try the dried yogurt?

882
00:23:32,160 --> 00:23:32,720
No.

883
00:23:32,720 --> 00:23:33,200
Try one.

884
00:23:33,200 --> 00:23:34,680
Don't lie to me.

885
00:23:34,680 --> 00:23:35,400
It's really good.

886
00:23:35,400 --> 00:23:36,120
Really?

887
00:23:37,240 --> 00:23:38,440
Eat it in one bite.

888
00:23:38,440 --> 00:23:39,520
It's too big. I can't.

889
00:23:42,840 --> 00:23:43,760
It's good, right?

890
00:23:43,760 --> 00:23:44,520
It's okay.

891
00:23:46,200 --> 00:23:47,440
Who is Kang?

892
00:23:47,440 --> 00:23:47,720
Kang.

893
00:23:47,720 --> 00:23:48,320
It should be you, right?

894
00:23:48,320 --> 00:23:51,400
Let's go.

895
00:23:52,000 --> 00:23:53,160
What did he just say?

896
00:23:53,160 --> 00:23:54,360
He said Kang.

897
00:23:56,080 --> 00:23:57,280
He said Ke.

898
00:23:57,600 --> 00:23:58,480
Ke.

899
00:23:59,000 --> 00:24:00,240
Ke. Ke.

900
00:24:01,480 --> 00:24:02,400
(Next Episode Preview)
That day, when we were

901
00:24:02,400 --> 00:24:03,520
(Solo mission experience)
going into the cabinet,

902
00:24:03,520 --> 00:24:05,000
I was hiding there by myself.

903
00:24:05,000 --> 00:24:05,800
I could hear

904
00:24:06,080 --> 00:24:08,360
them say, "3, 2, 1, scare him."

905
00:24:08,360 --> 00:24:09,840
If we have an escape room today,

906
00:24:09,840 --> 00:24:11,360
I'll be the first one to rush in.

907
00:24:11,720 --> 00:24:13,680
(Fully satisfied)
We'll definitely help you grow.

908
00:24:13,800 --> 00:24:15,680
Later, no one is allowed to...

909
00:24:15,680 --> 00:24:16,440
You know, one time we had

910
00:24:16,440 --> 00:24:17,640
